# mm.imu.qmi8658

The QST QMI8658 six-axis inertial sensor, over portable mm.mcu I2C. It contains
no vendor header and no board pin number: a board's provider supplies the wiring
and this module drives the protocol.

Registers are eight-bit, unlike the sixteen-bit map mm.touch.cst328 drives, so a
read is one address byte followed by the reply. It is still an mm.mcu
i2c_write_read rather than a write and a read, because the sensor's address
pointer must not be exposed to another master between the two halves.

Modelled on Waveshare's reference driver for the RP2350-Touch-LCD-2.8. Three
things in that driver are deliberately not reproduced. Its unit conversion is
absent, because mm.imu reports counts and a scale and lets the caller choose
units. Its AttitudeEngine, magnetometer, and wake-on-motion paths are absent,
because this board wires none of them and a driver should not carry registers
nobody can reach. Its address retry loop is kept, because the part answers at
one of two addresses and which one is a board fact the driver can discover
rather than demand.
